    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0001",
      "source": "ARKit provides the app with this reason when the app is in state [`ARGeoTrackingStatus.State.localizing`](argeotrackingstatus/state-swift.enum/localizing.md) and the device is not capturing enough of the necessary live-camera imagery needed for visual localization because the user is pointing the camera too low.",
      "ko": "This property returns a value in the range `0.0` to `1.0`, with `0.0` representing the minimum volume, and `1.0` representing the maximum volume.",
      "sourceHash": "75b00398141898ea369a817c38c4a822137427bcde6d32bfc65e4bfab1922a8c",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0008:0002",
      "source": "To resolve the issue, the app needs to instruct the user to raise the device and follow the guidance in [`Assisting the User with Visual Localization`](argeotrackingstatus/state-swift.enum/localizing#Assisting-the-User-with-Visual-Localization.md).",
      "ko": "이 문제를 해결하려면 앱이 사용자에게 기기를 올리라고 안내하고 [`Assisting the User with Visual Localization`](argeotrackingstatus/state-swift.enum/localizing#Assisting-the-User-with-Visual-Localization.md)의 지침을 따라야 합니다.",
      "sourceHash": "0d4d741e31468cb4809d7125c4af3218068ab95b40a32c2752b61c1720f9695c",
      "status": "machine_translated"
    },
